# Test-data and index artifacts — never commit these to the source repo.
# Reference panels, alignments, and truth/benchmark VCFs live OUTSIDE the repo
# (under data/ symlinks or /data/...). Only stray index files were ever committed
# by accident; this guard stops them (and the large data files) from coming back.

# Alignments + their indexes
*.bam
*.cram
*.bai
*.crai

# Variant/index files
*.csi
*.tbi
*.bcf

# GIAB / sample-specific test artifacts
HG002*
HG003*
HG004*

# Build output
/target/

# Internal working notes: kept locally, never pushed (the repository is public)
/docs/engineering/
/paper/internal_notes/

# Local benchmark inputs and individual-specific runners
/paper/benchmarks/private/

# Local run bundles and panel-distribution helpers (internal bucket names, large data)
/examples/*.tar.gz
/examples/manifest.tsv
/examples/presign_panel.sh
/examples/panel_urls.txt

# Manuscript: kept local only until submission (private history: /data/projects/selphi_paper_private.git)
/paper/*.md
/paper/*.docx
/paper/*.py
/paper/*.sh
/paper/figure1_pipeline.*
/paper/figures/
/paper/journals/
paper/benchmarks/fair_audit_2026_10/
